+\subsubsection{Version 0.14 evaluator-semantics note}
+
+%<*src_p0v14note>
+P0_V014_EVALUATOR_SEMANTICS
+
+Version 0.14 makes the five required local-evaluation checks operationally
+explicit and closes the finite candidate-hypothesis set under the four stated
+generation clauses.  In particular, satisfies_constraints is evaluation of
+all represented constraints over the completed candidate task state; for a
+same-relation constraint the relation committed to by the proposal support
+must hold on every represented successive position.  A correct output value
+does not validate an invalid derivation route.
+
+These clauses define validity rather than a preferred search algorithm.  A
+proposal need not coincide with a reference implementation's selected output
+to be valid, but it must be admitted by the active P0 candidate rules and pass
+all five required checks.  Version 0.14 adds no task identifier, expected
+answer, curriculum-stage condition, new proposal family, new KS object kind,
+or new construction mechanism.
+%</src_p0v14note>
